<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">4 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 4 May, from 1493 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1493">1493 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">533 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Alexander VI divides the Atlantic world</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inter-caetera">Inter caetera</a> drew a line west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azores">Azores</a>, granting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> lands beyond it. Portugal objected, and the line was moved further west by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tordesillas">Treaty of Tordesillas</a> in 1494.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tordesillas">Treaty of Tordesillas</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inter-caetera">Inter caetera</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/peter-minuit" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-minuit.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1626">1626 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">400 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Peter Minuit arrives in New Netherland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-minuit">Peter Minuit</a> reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a> as director of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colony. He soon bought the island from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lenape">Lenape</a> for goods worth 60 guilders, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a> became its capital.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-amsterdam">New Amsterdam</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rhode Island renounces allegiance to George III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rhode Island's assembly became the first colonial legislature to formally renounce allegiance to the Crown, two months before the Declaration of Independence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1799">1799 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">227 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tipu Sultan is killed as the British storm Seringapatam</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and allied troops breached the walls of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a>'s capital, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tipu-sultan">Tipu Sultan</a> died fighting at a gate. His defeat removed the strongest opponent of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1886">1886 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bomb explodes at a labour rally in Haymarket Square</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A bomb thrown at police in Chicago, and the gunfire that followed, killed seven officers and several civilians. Eight anarchists were convicted on thin evidence and four were hanged.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1904">1904 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">122 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">United States takes over the Panama Canal works</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US formally took possession of the abandoned French canal project. Completed in 1914, the canal spared ships the long voyage around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1970">1970 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">National Guard kills four students at Kent State</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a> National Guardsmen fired on students protesting the US invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a>, killing four and wounding nine. The shootings set off a nationwide student strike.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1979">1979 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">47 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Margaret Thatcher becomes Britain's first woman Prime Minister</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the Conservatives won the general election, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-thatcher">Margaret Thatcher</a> took office. In eleven years in power she privatised industries, curbed trade unions and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/falklands-war">Falklands War</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
